<% content_for :title, "Pricing" %>
<% content_for :description, "Free for one person and a gigabyte. Documents are unlimited on every plan, and alerts and renewal playbooks are never paywalled." %>

<h1>Pricing</h1>

<p class="lede">
  Storage is what costs us money, so storage is the only thing the plans limit. Documents are
  unlimited everywhere — recording that a marriage certificate exists is the point of the thing.
  <strong>Alerts and playbooks are never paywalled</strong> — putting the safety feature behind a
  card form would poison the trust the whole thing rests on.
</p>

<%# Annual rather than monthly, and not to look cheaper. A vault gets opened %>
<%# three times a year, and billing monthly for something you rarely touch %>
<%# gives twelve occasions a year to wonder whether you still need it. The %>
<%# rhythm this is bought on is the rhythm it should be paid on. %>
<div class="cards">
  <div class="card">
    <h3>Free</h3>
    <p class="headline">£0</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>1 person</li>
      <li><strong>1 GB</strong> — around 4,000 scans</li>
      <li>Unlimited documents</li>
      <li>Every alert</li>
      <li>Every renewal playbook</li>
      <li>Browser-side encryption</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Household</h3>
    <p class="headline">~£30<span class="note">/year</span></p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Up to 6 people</li>
      <li><strong>25 GB</strong></li>
      <li>Unlimited documents</li>
      <li>Shared alerts across the household</li>
      <li>Everything in Free</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Archive</h3>
    <p class="headline">~£70<span class="note">/year</span></p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Up to 6 people</li>
      <li><strong>100 GB</strong></li>
      <li>For decades of scanned paper</li>
      <li>Everything in Household</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h3>Self-hosted</h3>
    <p class="headline">£0</p>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Everything, on your own machine</li>
      <li>Storage is whatever your disk is</li>
      <li>One container</li>
      <li>Your data never touches us</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note"><a href="https://github.com/cdrrazan/Docaru">Run it yourself</a></p>
  </div>
</div>

<section>
  <h2>Why pay us rather than use a cloud drive</h2>
  <p>
    Because we cannot read your files, and Google can read theirs. Scans are encrypted in your
    browser with a key derived from a passphrase we never receive; what reaches us is ciphertext
    with no filename attached. That is not a promise about our conduct, it is a fact about the
    code — and <a href="https://github.com/cdrrazan/Docaru">the code is public</a>, so you can
    check rather than trust.
  </p>
  <p>
    It is also why we cannot offer search inside your documents, previews, or anything that reads
    them. Those features need a copy of your passport we are able to open. That trade is the
    product.
  </p>
  <p class="note">
    If you can run a container, self-hosting is stronger still, and it is free. We would rather say
    so than pretend otherwise.
  </p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2>What happens if you stop paying</h2>
  <p>
    You keep every document, every scan and every reminder. Nothing is deleted, nothing stops being
    watched, and no file becomes unreadable. What you lose is room to add more, until you are back
    under the free limits or back on a paid plan. Nobody misses a visa deadline over a failed card
    payment — that would be the product failing at the only job it has.
  </p>
</section>

<% if authenticated? %>
  <section>
    <h2>Your plan</h2>
    <p>
      <%= @household.name %> is on the <strong><%= @household.plan.humanize.downcase %></strong> plan,
      using <%= pluralize(@household.documents.count, "document") %> and
      <%= pluralize(@household.members.count, "person") %>.
    </p>

    <%= render "shared/storage", household: @household %>

    <% if (subscription = @household.subscription)&.troubled? %>
      <div class="banner banner-warn">
        <strong>There is a problem with the payment for this household.</strong>
        Paddle will retry the card over the next few days. <strong>Every reminder keeps
        working throughout</strong>, and it keeps working even if the payment never succeeds —
        nobody misses a visa deadline over a card.
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% if @household.over_storage_limit? || @household.over_member_limit? %>
      <div class="banner">
        This household is above the free limits. Nothing has been deleted and everything is still
        watched — you cannot add new scans or people until you are back under, or back on a paid
        plan.
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <% if @household.plan == "free" %>
      <% if Paddle.configured? %>
        <%= button_to "Upgrade to the household plan", plan_path, method: :patch, class: "btn" %>
        <p class="note">
          Checkout is handled by Paddle, who are the seller of record and will show the price in
          your own currency with any tax already included.
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <div class="banner">
          Billing is not switched on for this instance, so there is nothing behind this button and
          it is not shown. Every alert and every playbook works regardless — those are never
          paywalled.
        </div>
      <% end %>
    <% elsif subscription&.renews_on %>
      <p class="note">
        <%= subscription.canceled_at ? "Access continues until" : "Renews on" %>
        <%= subscription.renews_on.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %>.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
